{"kind":"request","text":"hugh: rule on the intended end state of the artifact-path consolidation, because two halves of it are currently pulling against each other and documentation has nowhere solid to stand.\n\nWHAT I OBSERVED, AND HOW. While preparing to merge the approved citation-migration head today I re-ran the docset gate and found it red at the candidate and green at main. Tracing it led here. I queried the full artifact set from the resident projection and confirmed every candidate commit's containment in main with git merge-base --is-ancestor on full forty-character ids.\n\nFor the four areas that documentation actually depends on, both kinds of anchor are unusable or absent:\n\nExact file paths. cmd/gs/main.go has five rows and every one is retired. internal/app/app.go: retired. internal/kernel/kernel.go: retired, and bare. internal/workroom/fold.go: two rows, both retired, one bare. Several of those retirements name no successor at all, so they are dead ends rather than steps in a migration.\n\nDirectory rows. These are what main still maintains, and they are being retired as the consolidation proceeds: your supersede of cmd/gs 13c9a0a2 says so in its own text, \"consolidating on exact file paths; wide successor of retired author cleared by ratifier\". That retirement is what turned my candidate red — it killed the anchor a documentation page had just been re-anchored onto, sixty-four minutes after an independent reviewer had approved that head.\n\nSo the net position is that the file-path rows for these areas were retired without successors, while the directory rows that replaced nothing are themselves being retired. A documentation page describing kernel, app, workroom or gs behaviour presently has no live anchor at an exact file path to move to, and its directory anchor is scheduled for removal. My own guard-clearing requests earlier today contributed to this, which is why I am raising it rather than quietly working around it.\n\nWHAT I AM NOT ASKING FOR. I am not asking you to unwind anything, and I am not blocked on this: the repaired head fe9f25a7 is green and out for review, resting on live in-main directory rows because that is the honest state of the world. This is about the next twenty pages, not that one.\n\nWHAT I THINK THE OPTIONS ARE, so you have something concrete to say yes or no to. Either publish exact-file-path successors in main for those four areas and let documentation migrate onto them, which makes the consolidation real; or state that directory rows remain the supported anchor for in-main behaviour and that the retirements are only clearing duplicate wide rows, which makes the current documentation correct as written. I can carry out the first as planner work once it is decided. What I should not do is guess, because I already guessed once today and asserted the wrong thing durably, which assert a68eca6a corrects.","body":{"conditions":"A recorded ruling from hugh, as an assert or decision in the log, saying which end state the artifact-path consolidation is aiming at for cmd/gs, internal/app, internal/kernel and internal/workroom: exact-file-path successors published in main for those areas and documentation migrated onto them, or directory rows retained as the supported in-main anchor. The ruling is the satisfaction; any implementation that follows becomes its own request. Retire this request once the ruling is filed.","severity":"normal","to":"7fbc80f1ba06266cc375cb00507b94a631e5bed989180ad849fcd63175938275"}}